  "body_html": "<h1>Strict Preference Relation</h1>\n<p>On any <code>Preorder α</code>, strict preference is the strict part of the preorder:\n$$\n  a \\succ b \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad a &lt; b\n  \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad a \\le b \\;\\text{ and }\\; \\neg(b \\le a).\n$$</p>\n<p>Strict preference is asymmetric, transitive, and irreflexive. These three\nproperties — asymmetry from <code>lt_asymm</code>, transitivity from <code>lt_trans</code>,\nirreflexivity from <code>lt_irrefl</code> — are inherited directly from the Mathlib\n<code>Preorder</code> API.</p>\n<p>In Lean this is <code>abbrev StrictlyPreferred (a b : α) : Prop := a &lt; b</code>. The\nabbreviation exists for readability in game-theory contexts; downstream code\nmay also use the bare <code>&lt;</code> notation interchangeably.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ, Chapter 2, Def. 2.5] Maschler, Solan, and Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>,\n  <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>. Strict preference derived from weak preference.</li>\n<li>[MSZ, Exercise 2.1(a)] Asymmetry, transitivity, and irreflexivity of strict\n  preference.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
